Mechanism/why it looks fine: Inter-VLAN routing on router0 is operating; frames from VLAN 20 are routed to VLAN 10 and vice versa. From laptop0 I can ping key hosts on 172.16.10.x with 0% loss and low RTT: PC4 (172.16.10.4) replies in ~1.0–1.7 ms and PC5 (172.16.10.5) in ~1.0–1.2 ms. Reverse direction also works: PC4 can ping 172.16.20.10 successfully. TTL values (~63) indicate exactly one L3 hop via router0, matching design. Wider checks also show other segments can reach PC4 normally.

Localization: The entire path laptop0 -> switch1/mswitch1 -> router0 (VLAN 20/10) -> switch1 -> PC4 is healthy; no interface, VLAN, or routing daemon issue observed.

Root cause: The reported outage cannot be reproduced now; no persistent network-side failure is present.

Corrective fix: No network changes required. If the issue recurs, capture exact time and whether name vs. IP access fails; on the client, clear ARP/DNS caches or reboot, and check for host firewalls or duplicate IPs on 172.16.20.x. We will monitor for intermittents. 
